{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Establish a persistent integrity baseline for regular files under /etc on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A root-only SHA-256 manifest containing 278 /etc files was initialized and immediately matched a fresh check. The checker, manifest, and scheduled job retained identical hashes after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e761b25b66ff4b4b","cmd-67fded12de7644c4","cmd-0326992e310d4fd1","cmd-b9ffa3c80d03429f"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Provide a way for later changes under /etc to be identified and reported.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The checker directly detected and reported both an added file and modified /etc/issue content, returned a drift status, and returned to a clean result after each test change was restored. Daily execution was installed and crond was enabled and observed running after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-83f3fa742c8743c0","cmd-df44fc29705347bf","cmd-4b83ad10953f4b63","cmd-b9ffa3c80d03429f"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.86,"summary":"The final system was healthy and the integrity-test mutations were bounded and fully restored. Two hygiene issues remain: cmd-7eb4d267690846f7 refreshed APK indexes while attempting an AIDE installation that failed and did not contribute to the final implementation; no rollback or cache cleanup was captured, so whether all resulting cache state remained is uncertain. The required restart command cmd-0ea631cc034648e4 also created /tmp/etc-integrity-reboot.log, which remained after execution and was unnecessary residue. No new network exposure or package-health degradation was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7eb4d267690846f7","cmd-0ea631cc034648e4","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcomes are satisfied. Node1 has a persistent SHA-256 baseline for /etc and a working checker that directly demonstrated change reporting and clean restoration. Restart evidence is complete: it includes pre-restart identity and health, acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovered crond, checker, and unchanged baseline state; fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Removed-file detection was not directly exercised, although the manifest-diff implementation supports it and added-file and modified-file behavior were directly demonstrated.","The lifecycle failed-service probe used systemctl and was unsupported on Alpine; crond health was nevertheless checked directly before and after restart.","The retained effects, if any, of the APK index refresh were not captured in enough detail to determine complete cleanup."]}
